From: Josep Maria Blasco <josep.maria.blasco@epbcn.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:40:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] WebAssembly port: build variants for the test suite's
 native libraries

The API test groups of the test suite (API/classic, API/oo) load the
native libraries of testbinaries/, and two of them run
testbinaries/rexxinstance as a command; with no dlopen in WebAssembly,
none of their tests could run.  wasm/build-test.sh [BUILD_DIR]
[node|web|both] builds, for testing only, variants of the two relinked
builds with those libraries linked in (BUILD_DIR/bin-node-test,
BUILD_DIR/bin-web-test):

- the libraries are compiled as they are and described by the table
  orx_wasm_static_libraries() that SysLibrary looks up (patch 1/6); the
  names more than one library defines get a prefix per library, mapped
  back in the table, and the API macros that put a name in a method or
  routine table are redefined to keep the name as written;
- rexxinstance is one more tool in the Node variant's rexx.wasm, as rexxc
  is (rexx.js --orx-wasm-rexxinstance, and a launcher), through a weak
  hook in rexx.cpp's dispatcher, orxWasmExtraTool();
- build-node.sh and build-web.sh link EXTRA_OBJECTS.

With them, the eight API groups pass under Node and in the browsers, as
natively (796 tests).  The standard builds are unchanged.
