+## The test suite's API groups (`wasm/build-test.sh`)
+
+The API test groups of the ooRexx test suite (`API/classic`, `API/oo`) load
+the native libraries of `testbinaries/` (`orxfunction`, `orxmethod`,
+`orxclassic`, `orxclassic1`, `orxexits`, `orxinvocation`), and two of them
+run `testbinaries/rexxinstance` as a command.  There is no `dlopen` in
+WebAssembly, so `wasm/build-test.sh [BUILD_DIR] [node|web|both]` builds
+variants of the two relinked builds with those libraries linked in, for
+testing only: `BUILD_DIR/bin-node-test` (with `rexxinstance` as one more
+tool of `rexx.wasm`, as `rexxc` is) and `BUILD_DIR/bin-web-test`.
+
+The libraries are described by a table, `orx_wasm_static_libraries()`, that
+`SysLibrary` looks up before `dlopen`/`dlsym` (a weak symbol: absent in the
+standard builds), so `::METHOD ... EXTERNAL "LIBRARY orxmethod ..."`,
+`RxFuncAdd(..., 'orxclassic1', ...)` and `RexxRegister*Dll(...)` find them
+unchanged.  The libraries define some of the same names; the script gives
+those a prefix per library and maps them back in the table.  Run the groups
+from the test suite's directory:
+
+```sh
+BUILD_DIR/bin-node-test/rexx testOORexx.rex -R ooRexx/API
+```
+
 ## Known limitations / deliberate non-claims
 
 * WebSocket transport (browser, and the MEMFS build under Node): listening
